From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@y>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 01:59:31 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] llama: replace the shortconv recurrent-state gather with a
 cache view when the slot mapping is identity

Port of the R9700/HIP track patch 0011 to the GB10 CUDA series. The patch is
core C++ only -- src/llama-graph, src/llama-memory-recurrent, src/models/lfm2 --
and contains no backend code, so it applies to the CUDA tree unchanged.

Every LFM2.5 shortconv layer materializes its conv window before the block runs:
build_rs gathers it with k_get_rows_float, purely to move 16 KB to a new address
so the next kernel can read it. The gather exists for seq-copy migration and
rollback-snapshot restore; during steady single-slot decode its ids are the
identity.

The identity case is detected side-effect-free at graph build time
(llama_memory_recurrent_context::s_copy_main_is_identity: cells[head+i].src0 ==
head+i with no pending rollback restore) and the gather is replaced by a
contiguous ggml_view_2d of the cache rows. Byte-identical values reach the
consumer and the get_rows kernel disappears.

Reuse safety: the fork reuses built graphs across decode steps and a view bakes
its offset at build time while get_rows refreshes through the s_copy input
tensor. The view is therefore restricted to the single-slot serving shape
(n_seqs == 1, head == 0, n_rs == 1), where the baked offset is row 0 always --
which is the ranked configuration (--parallel 1). Multi-slot, migrated or
rollback states fall back to the stock gather.

Measured on GB10 (sm_121, CUDA 13.0, LFM2.5-2.6B-Q4_K_M), against a build of the
13-patch parent series:

  - census: k_get_rows_float falls from 24 to 2 launches per decoded token.
  - decode tg128, isolated on one binary with LLAMA_DISABLE_RS_STATE_VIEW:
    120.74 -> 121.24, +0.41%.
  - perplexity bit-identical on both shapes (22.7466 gate, 22.6048 decode-path).

It also does something for the shortconv fold in the next patch that no
backend-side check can: with the window living in the persistent recurrent cache
instead of a compute-buffer temporary, the fold's state source can no longer
alias the block its own output lands on, so the fold's disjointness test passes
on many more layers. The two together measure +1.64%, against 0.41% and 0.66%
alone -- the gain is superadditive by construction.

LLAMA_DISABLE_RS_STATE_VIEW=1 restores the stock gather everywhere.
---
 src/llama-graph.cpp            | 34 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 src/llama-graph.h              |  6 ++++--
 src/llama-memory-recurrent.cpp | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 src/llama-memory-recurrent.h   |  5 +++++
 src/models/lfm2.cpp            |  2 +-
 5 files changed, 56 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/llama-graph.cpp b/src/llama-graph.cpp
index e12a8cdc..dd50a0eb 100644
--- a/src/llama-graph.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-graph.cpp
@@ -3287,7 +3287,8 @@ ggml_tensor * llm_graph_context::build_rs(
            uint32_t   rs_head,
            uint32_t   rs_size,
             int32_t   rs_zero,
-        const llm_graph_get_rows_fn & get_state_rows) const {
+        const llm_graph_get_rows_fn & get_state_rows,
+              bool   state_is_identity) const {
 
     GGML_UNUSED(rs_size);
     ggml_tensor * states = ggml_reshape_2d(ctx0, s, state_size, s->ne[1]);
@@ -3300,7 +3301,19 @@ ggml_tensor * llm_graph_context::build_rs(
     // copy states
     // NOTE: assuming the copy destinations are ALL contained between rs_head and rs_head + n_rs
     // {state_size, rs_size} -> {state_size, n_seqs}
-    ggml_tensor * output_states = get_state_rows(ctx0, states, state_copy_main);
+    // When every source row is the destination row itself (steady-state decode:
+    // no seq-copy migration, no rollback-snapshot restore - detected side-effect-
+    // free at graph build time), the gather is a pure materialization of rows
+    // [rs_head, rs_head + n_seqs) and is replaced by a contiguous view of the
+    // cache: byte-identical values reach the consumer and the per-layer state
+    // copy disappears. The view keeps the same execution-order reliance on the
+    // rs_zero clear that the get_rows form already has.
+    ggml_tensor * output_states;
+    if (state_is_identity) {
+        output_states = ggml_view_2d(ctx0, states, state_size, n_seqs, states->nb[1], rs_head*states->nb[1]);
+    } else {
+        output_states = get_state_rows(ctx0, states, state_copy_main);
+    }
     ggml_build_forward_expand(gf, output_states);
 
     // copy extra states which won't be changed further (between n_seqs and n_rs)
@@ -3348,12 +3361,25 @@ ggml_tensor * llm_graph_context::build_rs(
         ggml_tensor * s,
             int32_t   state_size,
             int32_t   n_seqs,
-        const llm_graph_get_rows_fn & get_state_rows) const {
+        const llm_graph_get_rows_fn & get_state_rows,
+              bool   allow_state_view) const {
     const auto * kv_state = inp->mctx;
 
+    // Reuse safety: a built graph bakes the view offset while the fork reuses
+    // graphs across decode steps (only ~27 builds serve a 256-token completion
+    // here), so the view is additionally restricted to the single-slot serving
+    // shape (n_seqs == 1, head == 0, n_rs == 1). There the baked offset is row 0
+    // always - a reused view graph can never go stale - and this is exactly the
+    // ranked serving configuration (--parallel 1), so the full decode gain is
+    // kept. Multi-slot or migrated states fall back to the stock gather.
+    static const bool disable_state_view = getenv("LLAMA_DISABLE_RS_STATE_VIEW") != nullptr;
+    const bool state_is_identity = allow_state_view && !disable_state_view &&
+        n_seqs == 1 && kv_state->get_head() == 0 && kv_state->get_n_rs() == 1 &&
+        kv_state->s_copy_main_is_identity(n_seqs);
+
     return build_rs(s, inp->s_copy_main, inp->s_copy_extra, state_size, n_seqs,
                     kv_state->get_n_rs(), kv_state->get_head(), kv_state->get_size(), kv_state->get_rs_z(),
-                    get_state_rows);
+                    get_state_rows, state_is_identity);
 }
 
 ggml_tensor * llm_graph_context::build_rwkv_token_shift_load(
diff --git a/src/llama-graph.h b/src/llama-graph.h
index 160e2941..b67d2d1f 100644
--- a/src/llama-graph.h
+++ b/src/llama-graph.h
@@ -1256,7 +1256,8 @@ struct llm_graph_context {
                uint32_t   rs_head,
                uint32_t   rs_size,
                 int32_t   rs_zero,
-            const llm_graph_get_rows_fn & get_state_rows = ggml_get_rows) const;
+            const llm_graph_get_rows_fn & get_state_rows = ggml_get_rows,
+                   bool   state_is_identity = false) const;
 
     llm_graph_input_rs * build_rs_inp() const;
 
@@ -1265,7 +1266,8 @@ struct llm_graph_context {
             ggml_tensor * s,
                 int32_t   state_size,
                 int32_t   n_seqs,
-            const llm_graph_get_rows_fn & get_state_rows = ggml_get_rows) const;
+            const llm_graph_get_rows_fn & get_state_rows = ggml_get_rows,
